<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04235/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04235/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S04/current/S04235/>;
    dc:modified '2019-08-02T14:20:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ICP-AES'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'inductively-coupled plasma atomic emission spectroscopy'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Also sometimes referred to as inductively-coupled plasma optical emission spectroscopy (ICP-OES). A sample is passed through a nebulizer to create an aerosol and transported via an argon gas stream to an inductively-coupled gas plasma (8-10000 K) where it is dried, melted, evaporated, atomized, then excited. The excited atoms pass through the cooler part of the plasma and de-excite releasing specific-wavelength photons dependent on the element. Emissions are passed to the optical system which measures their intensities, which are directly proportional to the concentrations of the analytes.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S04::S04235'^^xsd:string .
